# muster: the closed list of states of the machine "one muster, from the depth pick to a released and proven build".
# value<TAB>mark (initial, final or -)<TAB>kind (active, waiting, rest, final)<TAB>meaning
triage	initial	active	the depth is picked and no round has been asked yet
discover	-	active	War Room researches the raw idea and a critic reviews the findings for round 1
council	-	active	specialist lenses argue first and their questions merge into round 1
intent	-	active	the why, the people and the end state are being agreed (docs/vision.md)
lexicon	-	active	the shared language is being written (GLOSSARY.md with the core objects)
rules	-	active	the stack, lint, comments, folders and tests are being written as rules with checks
terrain	-	active	the domain model and the hard decisions are being written (model, design, real ADRs)
sand-table	-	active	cheap prototypes are being picked for screens and flows
charter	-	active	what is delivered, and in which order, is being written (docs/charter.md)
objectives	-	active	the proof journeys are written and wait for a pack check on the base
check	-	active	the program has checked the pack and written the manifest; no approval is asked yet
approval	-	active	the captain is asked to approve this exact checked pack
war-room	-	active	the pack is approved and the plan is being made from the charter
blitz	-	active	the build is under way and at least one objective has no receipt on the landed commit
landed	-	active	every objective has a receipt on the landed commit and no release record names it
secured	final	final	every objective has a receipt on the landed commit, the model's behaviour is in the code and a release names it
